1. She has experience with fast typing and note-taking from working in an office environment. (Verbatim: "i had to type fast-ish to keep up with it um and the same with like um if i had a lecture that wasn't recorded i'd have to try and yeah speed type")

2. She used to take notes in meetings primarily to avoid participating in conversations. (Verbatim: "the only reason i wanted to take notes in meetings was because i didn't want to listen in the meetings... you just have to focus on transcribing the words so you don't actually have to really listen")

3. She attended university (or college) and struggled with lectures, often feeling overwhelmed by gaps in knowledge. (Verbatim: "i remember having that feeling in lectures being like i don't even know what to ask at this point")

4. She experienced being misled about course content not being on exams, only to find it on the test. (Verbatim: "they're like oh they changed it this year and i'm like oh okay good day now")

5. She bought expensive textbooks for university that she never used, which now serve as paperweights. (Verbatim: "i still have those books on my shelf i ain't ever read them i ain't ever touched them... very good paperweights")

6. She identifies as a socially awkward introvert who struggles with group activities and social battery. (Verbatim: "i am a socially awkward introvert... extrovert elia... can't hold extrovert elia up very much... she runs out of battery")

7. She tried joining the anime society at university but left after one meeting due to anxiety and exhaustion. (Verbatim: "i tried to join the anime one and i went once and then i never returned because it drained me too much")

8. She found collaborative note-taking helpful, using shared Google Docs with classmates to transcribe lectures. (Verbatim: "we had a google doc of the notes of the lecture and with the combined power of multiple people we'd be able to to get a good proper transcription")

